        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# A Repeating Texture Tile\n\nGenerates a square texture that tiles without visible seams, for backgrounds and surfaces. The prompt asks for tiling explicitly, because a texture without matching edges shows a seam as soon as it repeats.\n\n**How it works:** \"1 Prompt\" describes hand-made paper as a tileable, top-down texture. \"2 Generate\" renders it at 1:1 and 1K resolution. \"3 Image\" shows the tile.\n\n**Try this:** Pick a model on \"2 Generate\" and replace the paper with another material, such as worn concrete or linen, keeping the words about tiling and seams."
        },
